
The tool set is what the design says, and bash is deliberately absent
  ok   read, write, edit and a shell are bundled
  ok   no bash tool — native-Windows bash is an undeclared Git Bash dependency
  ok   a verifier loses write and edit

cli.mjs actually installs and scopes them (an uninstalled control is not a control)
  ok   the guard is installed
  ok   the seat tools are installed
  ok   the harness is given the confining environment
  ok   the roster is filled from the store
  ok   seat tools are scoped at `up`

The tool set follows each seat's DECLARED CAPABILITIES, so routing is enforced by capability (F9)
  ok   an implementer keeps every working tool
  ok   a coordinator loses read, write, edit AND the shell, so it can only route
  ok   a verifier loses write and edit but keeps read and the shell, so it can still re-run
  ok   a seat declaring NOTHING is treated as a coordinator - fail closed for tools, and check reports it

The environment chosen per seat — and it fails CLOSED
  ok   an author seat can write inside its root
  ok   a verifier seat cannot write, whatever tools it was offered
  ok   an unknown conversation fails closed (read-only), not open
  ok   every seat's environment is rooted, so an escape is refused even for an author

The roster reuses `check`'s verifier judgement rather than inventing a second one
  ok   an author is not marked a verifier
  ok   a qa seat is
  ok   an editor seat is (the same vocabulary `check` uses)

PASS — the controls are wired

